  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $9\\,\\text{ft},$ $4\\,\\text{ft},$ and $5\\,\\text{ft},$ respectively?",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9\\,\\text{ft},\\,w=4\\,\\text{ft},\\,h=5\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=9\\cdot 4\\cdot 5=180\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$",
